==== M569.4: Set Motor Driver Force Mode ====
{{Firmware Support | fived={{no}} | teacup={{no}} | sprinter={{no}} | marlin={{no}} | prusa={{no}} | repetier={{no}} | smoothie={{no}} | reprapfirmware={{yes}}<sup>1</sup> | bfb={{no}} | grbl={{no}} | makerbot={{no}} | machinekit={{no}} | redeem={{no}} | mk4duo={{no}} | yaskawa={{no}} }}

Tell one or more motor drivers to apply a specified force regardless of position.

;Parameters
:<code>Pn</code> or <code>Pn.n</code> Motor driver number, or board address and driver number. Can also be a colon separated list of driver numbers.
:<code>Tn</code> Where n is the mode/force to apply in units of Newtons.

If <code>P</code> or <code>T</code> parameter is missing, then no action is taken.
The driver is put back into position mode by requesting a force smaller than 0.0001 N.

;Examples
 M569.4
<tt>Error: M569: missing parameter 'P'</tt>
 M569.4 P40.0:41.0
<tt>Error: M569: missing parameter 'T'</tt>
 M569.4 P40.0 T0.001
<tt>0.001000 Nm,</tt>
 M569.4 P40.0:41.0 T0
<tt>pos_mode, pos_mode,</tt>

;Notes
Hangprinter's "force mode" is implemented as a ReprapFirmware macro that depends on M569.4.

Practical forces for tightening lines in daily use tend to lie between 15 N and 25 N for a Hangprinter.
